ext=("Diphenhydramine is absorbed well and crosses easily into the brain, unlike newer antihistamines.","Blocking histamine H1 receptors causes sedation; blocking muscarinic receptors causes dry mouth, flushing, wide pupils, urinary retention and fast heart rate.","At high levels, muscarinic blockade in the brain causes delirium, and sodium channel blockade in the heart widens the QRS complex, risking fatal arrhythmias.","Seizures are common in severe poisoning; overheating occurs because sweating stops.","Delirium can outlast the drowsiness by many hours.","Chronic use in older adults is linked to cognitive decline and is on the Beers list of drugs to avoid."),
